    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d224">

                <pb facs="0370" n="276" xml:id="pg276"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6831/45: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-11-19T16:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 19,
                                1924—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>104. When I carried out the instructions contained in your number 81 November 10,
                    6 p.m.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d224-f1"/> Snipesos [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Roussos</hi>] said that the Greek Government had decided to apply minimum
                    tariff rates for three months after December 10 pending conclusion of new treaty
                    and that this time might be extended if negotiations were not then concluded. He
                    said he had already telegraphed Greek Legation to communicate this to you.</p>
                <p>On looking over your proposed draft he added that it seemed to him to follow the
                    lines acceptable to his Government and that he would hasten the consultations
                    necessary for acting upon it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d224-f1" n="19" xml:id="d224-f1-content">
                <p>“81. Department’s 80, November 8, 3 P.M. Please informally give to the Foreign
                    Office a copy of the text of Department’s note to the Charge d’Affaires of
                    Greece, replying to his note No. 934 of September 10, as well as the text of the
                    draft note proposed for exchange. Hughes.” (File no. 611.6831/43.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
